{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792891331,"nonce":"vwMuMfZq25e9BfAZ03sTFvyJ3oo=","title":"Reopening extension sidebars leaves the readiness loader spinning","message":"Opening the Git SCM sidebar a second time can leave its loading overlay spinning forever. StudioView evaluates readiness before attaching its surface. Closing the last surface releases Preview nodes but retains the model; attach recreates those nodes, yet hasView observes only incoming extension operations through elements. An unchanged Git refresh emits no new operations, so the recreated surface never invalidates the waiting overlay or disabled tools.\n\nReproduce with a static delayed extension by opening its sidebar, waiting for readiness, hiding it and reopening without new script operations. Add regression coverage for repeated show/hide, retained models, tool readiness and the real Git extension; verify resource cleanup and startup/failure feedback remain correct.","files":null}]}